# cmd.exe is not reliable on LF-only batch files: goto and multi-line
# parenthesised blocks can misparse, and both scripts here use both.
# The release workflow runs publish.cmd on a GitHub runner, where the
# checkout's autocrlf setting is not ours to control - so pin it here
# instead of hoping.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# release.ps1 is UTF-8 with a BOM: Windows PowerShell 5.1 decodes a BOM-less
# .ps1 using the local codepage, which turns every Chinese prompt into
# mojibake. The text attribute only pins line endings, it never touches the
# BOM - so this is safe. Pin CRLF to match how the file was written.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The workflow is read by GitHub, not by cmd.exe. Keep it LF so the file
# stops flip-flopping between checkouts on a machine with autocrlf on.
*.yml text eol=lf
